    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1376">

                <pb facs="1071" n="955" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg955"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/909.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Vice Consul Davis</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 239.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 27, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your despatch
                    No. 621 dated November 5, 1915, setting forth the arbitrary manner in which
                    mining interests are being treated by the present de facto government in
                    Mexico.</p>
                <p>A copy of your despatch has been sent to Mr. Charles B. Parker, who is acting in
                    representation of American interests at Mexico <pb facs="1072" n="956"
                        xml:id="pg956"/> City, Mexico, with instructions to bring the statements
                    contained therein to the attention of the appropriate authorities, in connection
                    with previous representations, and earnestly to continue his efforts for a
                    material modification of the decree imposing increased taxes upon mining
                    properties.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Acting Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilbur J. Carr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
